OL,3,GNEWSAFootball clubs unite for player
OL,4,Awith brain tumour
OL,5,
OL,6,FTwo women's football teams came
OL,7,Ftogether in support of "one of their
OL,8,Fown", a player who is currently
OL,9,Fundergoing treatment for a brain
OL,10,Ftumour.
OL,12,FRoxy Thomas, 18, who plays for Torquay
OL,13,FUnited Women, remains in intensive care
OL,14,Fin Bristol after a series of operations
OL,15,Ffollowing her diagnosis in August.
OL,17,FTorquay faced her former club Plymouth
OL,18,FArgyle in a Women's National League Cup
OL,19,Ffixture on Sunday. Argyle said it would
OL,20,Fdonate all of the gate receipts to a
OL,21,Ffundraiser set up to support her and
OL,22,Fher family.
OL,23,APub: 28-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
